/-!
# Graded observers

Observers graded by bounded pseudometrics, with a declared sampling measure,
on top of the observer classes and the theory–model connection.

* `Cybernetics.DistinctionCalculus.Ledger`: expected indistinction as an exact
  ledger (increments, strictness on the support, Markov and sup bounds,
  telescoping along chains); the valuation law, and on metric tolerances and
  equivalence relations its forced-completion defect; the closure of a crisp
  seed is its equivalence closure, so joins of equivalence relations are
  decidable on finite carriers. `LedgerControls`: `1/3, 5/9, 1`; `17/25`
  against `29/50`; the forced masses `2/9` and `2/15`.
* `Cybernetics.DistinctionCalculus.GradedCongruence`: graded congruences for a
  monoid of contexts on a fragment; the least one above a seed (a reflection;
  for crisp seeds, the generated congruence, hence decidable); the greatest one
  protecting declared consumers (the all-continuation discrepancy, equal to
  `1 − d_F` under the consumer guard, with the coarsest congruence inside the
  kernel of the consumers as its zero kernel); the feasible interval between
  the generated and the observational end. `GradedCongruenceControls`: no
  greatest decodable quotient; protection must be metric; thresholds are not
  transitive; generated strictly inside observational; the consumer guard is
  needed.
* `Cybernetics.DistinctionCalculus.PreservationGrade`: one- and two-sided
  preservation grades in Łukasiewicz form, their composition, collapse; a
  metric tolerance as a Mathlib pseudometric space on a type synonym.
* `Logic.TheoryModel.ExpectedWeakness`: expected indistinction is the expected
  mass of a random structure's class, bounded by the expected model mass of its
  observed theory, with equality under separation and negation; the bubble
  instance through Hennessy–Milner formulas; crisp closure computes equational
  consequences; the quantale weakness is a peak, the expectation a valuation.
* `Logic.TheoryModel.EpsilonHosting`: testing pseudometrics from sentence
  weightings, hosting up to `ε`, the leak bound, zero hosting as twins and as
  faithfulness on tested sentences. `EpsilonHostingControls`: reducts are
  isometries; the collapsing and representative comorphisms; the identity-proof
  ladder; faithful hosting is not zero hosting.
* `GSLT.Logic.GradedSupport`: graded rewriting over a semiring; support
  adequacy in every semiring; conservativity when the algebra cannot cancel;
  cancellation over the integers and the xor ring; end normalisation against
  the jump chain; the jump chain and the uniformised chain.
* `GSLT.Logic.GradedObserverBridge`: the congruence generated by stipulations
  against a bubble's equality (βη complete, sealed strict); a grade is a
  readout, never permission to substitute.
-/
